==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Has high damage.
* Has high mobility.
** All moves can be used as movement, even its M1 move.
* Can also damage [[Rubber]] users.
* Easy to grind [[mastery]] with it because of its high damage and fast M1s.
* Good combo potential.
* All moves have low end-lag, making it hard to punish.
* All moves are able to ''multi-hit'' targets.
* All moves can damage [[Sea Beast]]s, even though {{Ability|C}} can fling the user into the [[water]].
* Good for [[Buddha]] users because if the player uses an auto-clicker, they can click extremely fast and the moves are pretty good as well.
* Performs exceptionally well with screen-shake turned off, further increasing its effectiveness.

|'''[Z] Electric Rampage'''
* High stun. (When held.)
* Low cooldown.

|'''[X] Lightning Thrust'''
* Easy to land.
* High range.

|'''[C] Thunderclap and Flash'''
* Easy to land.
* Amazing for fighting skycampers. When used in air, it slams them to the ground.
* Auto-aiming feature, similar to [[Venom]] [X] and [[Godhuman]] [C].
* High range.
* Has a really fast movement speed.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Difficult to obtain as the player needs 400 mastery on [[Electric]], {{Money|3,000,000}} and {{Fragment|5,000}} and needs to be in [[Third Sea]].
* A bit of a disadvantage in during AFK farming or grinding because of the M1 dash, though this can be circumvented by moving around the player in a circle while moving the pointer to face the enemy. 
* High mastery requirements.
* Weak in air.

|'''[Z] Electric Rampage'''
* Short range.
* Can be punished if the opponent is fast enough.
* Barrage has low damage only the final hit deals the most damage. Meaning the enemy can escape the full attack and deal less damage.

|'''[X] Lightning Thrust'''
* High knockback.

|'''[C] Thunderclap and Flash'''
* Can be a disadvantage when fighting in the sea unless if the user has [[Shark]] race.
* Bounces the enemy sideways instead of upwards if used to hit an airborne enemy, reducing the combo potential.
* Despite possessing 'auto-aim', it in reality has a set path in which it can 'snag' opponents, therefore it is not guaranteed to connect, and requires practice to memorize the dashes.
* Requires aim and speed to use accurately.
}}
</tabber>

